# Where `@cyka/ui` comes from. It is a private package in the group's registry on
# lab, so the scope needs an address and a token, and both belong beside the
# manifest that names it rather than on whatever machine happens to build here.
#
# **The group endpoint, not the instance one.** GitLab's instance-wide npm
# endpoint only answers for a scope spelled the same as the root namespace, and
# the scope is `@cyka` while the group is `acyka`.
#
# `CYKA_NPM_TOKEN` is the group's `npm read` deploy token — read on the package
# registry and nothing else — so this file holds no secret and is committed.
@cyka:registry=https://lab.cyka.cloud/api/v4/groups/acyka/-/packages/npm/
//lab.cyka.cloud/api/v4/groups/acyka/-/packages/npm/:_authToken=${CYKA_NPM_TOKEN}
